{
  "biological_interpretation": "Direct loss of proteasome core, 19S ATPase, or maturation activity is not a benign compensatory proteasome upshift; in vulnerable neurons it pairs proteasome recovery signatures with loss of ion-channel, receptor, and mature neuronal expression.",
  "caveats": [
    "Pomp, Psmc1, and Psmc5 target-transcript depletion was often not FDR-confirmed, so downstream signatures should not be scaled as mRNA knockdown dose responses.",
    "This is a broad proteasome-stress axis and should not be used to nominate a single safe proteasome subunit to inhibit."
  ],
